  "release_notes": "New: \"Ask Minis\" via Siri — say \"Hey Siri, Ask Minis\" to jump straight into a live conversation.\n\nNew: Kimi Code sign-in support, plus full OAuth login for MCP servers (with iCloud config sync across devices).\n\nNew: Codex Fast Mode toggle for OpenAI OAuth models.\n\nNew: Live Activity (privacy mode) now shows real task progress — position, status, and run time.\n\nNew: Select any text and tap \"Read Aloud\" to hear it via Minis TTS. Voice correction learning now uses real conversation context, further improving correction accuracy.\n\nNew: Max output length raised from 64K to 128K tokens. In-browser downloads got a full UX overhaul with floating progress cards and a downloads panel.\n\nStability: Fixed several stability issues in message streaming, Live Activity restore on iPad, HealthKit data reads, and config loading after a device restart. Reduced stutter during long \"thinking\" streams and scrolling.\n\nBug fixes:\n- Markdown tables keep their scroll position while streaming\n- Fixed duplicate thinking bubbles on retry\n- Fixed invisible scroll buttons in light mode\n- Fixed navbar title staying blurred after Face ID unlock\n- Session list timestamps are properly localized\n- Fixed in-app browser fetch failures\n- Fixed Mistral chat compatibility issue\n- Backfilled translations for ~200 previously English-only strings\n- Added Claude Opus 5 to the built-in model list\n- Fixed occasional config or chat history issues after a device restart\n- Fixed occasional unresponsiveness when checking Now Playing info or using speech synthesis\n- Fixed regenerating a session title not following the latest model order\n- Fixed some health metric types occasionally being skipped when reading HealthKit data\n- Fixed onboarding setup steps missing translations in some languages\n- Reduced app install size",
